# Claude ↔ Cursor workflow

Planning shape matches `~/Dev/ai-project-kit/WORKFLOW.md`, without treating
every kit ceremony as mandatory.

## Shared brain (non-negotiable)

Both tools use repo files, not each other's chat history:

`AGENTS.md` · `PRODUCT_SSOT_SLJAKAM.md` · `PROJECT_SSOT.md` · `PROGRESS.md` ·
`NEEDS_STEFAN.md` · `docs/refactor/MIGRATION_PLAN.md`

If a decision matters later, write it into one of those files (decisions go
in `PROGRESS.md` → Decisions).

## Ownership

- **One owner per phase** (Cursor or Claude or Stefan), recorded in
  `PROGRESS.md`.
- Don't edit the same files in parallel without an explicit owner switch
  recorded in `PROGRESS.md`.
- Parallel agents need separate branches/worktrees and separate ports/DBs/
  test users (`pnpm e2e` already uses its own `<db>_e2e` database and Redis
  DB 15).

## Default roles (flexible)

| Role                                                                                                           | Usually                               |
| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Options, product trade-offs, schema, auth, billing, search, sync, test harness, acceptance tests, PR review, deploy | Claude Code                           |
| UI phases, CRUD following an existing module, making Claude's acceptance tests pass, iteration, polish          | Cursor                                |
| Serbian-language copy drafts and research (legal research, copy review)                                         | ChatGPT (draft only; Stefan approves) |
| Full phase end-to-end                                                                                          | Either — only one                     |

## Session hygiene

- Prefer one chat per phase or clear topic.
- End sessions by updating `PROGRESS.md`.
- Every non-trivial request should state **done means** and **what must not
  change** (or ask Stefan to confirm).

## Quality bar

- Show whole-repo check output before calling work done.
- New behaviour gets a test that failed before the fix (`e2e/` for flows a
  person clicks through, Vitest for pure logic).
- UI checked at phone and desktop widths.
- No commit/push on red checks. A finished phase is pushed, merged after
  green CI and deployed (Stefan's standing instruction); otherwise commit
  only when Stefan asks.
